  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Anglican Alliance climate, peacebuilding and advocacy</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Objectives
1)&#xA0;&#xA0;&#xA0;&#xA0; Protecting the planet and communities living on the front line of climate change. We particularly recognise and affirm the role of young people in advocating for the safeguarding of creation and for adequate climate finance. 
2)&#xA0;&#xA0;&#xA0;&#xA0; Supporting churches and their communities to build resilience and preparedness before disaster strikes, including by sharing security advice and localised expertise, sharing research, evidence, and learning to strengthen our practical faith engagement strategies in order to bring about system change. 
3)&#xA0;&#xA0;&#xA0;&#xA0; We will specifically look at shifting beliefs, attitudes and practices (among individuals, and within communities and religious institutions) to promote equality, protect communities, reduce violence and transform conflict.</narrative>
  </description>
